## Twitter / Thread-Friendly Description (copy-paste)

> ⚙️ Building an AI trader that can't bypass its own risk controls.
> 
> Most AI trading systems: "Trade first, ask questions never." ❌
> 
> This project: "Risk gate first, log always." ✅
> 
> The **Risk Gate** sits between the AI signal generator and execution layer. The AI **cannot** bypass position limits, daily loss limits, or confidence thresholds. It's the Wall Street principle made code.
> 
> Five governance modules, wired into the loop:
> 1️⃣ Pre-signal data integrity — catches stale/NaN feeds **before** signal generation
> 2️⃣ Curator profile selector — allowlist, cooldown, auto-revert on underperformance
> 3️⃣ Atomic multi-leg execution — delta-neutral packages with enforced slippage limits
> 4️⃣ Strategy validation — walk-forward, PBO, Calmar/Sharpe gates (Calmar ≥ 1.0 AND PBO ≤ 0.5)
> 5️⃣ Local append-only audit log — JSONL recording every governance decision
> 
> Every decision is signed with EIP-191 and submitted to **TradeAuditTrail.sol on X Layer****before** the order hits OKX. If logging fails, trading is blocked.
> 
> **343 tests, fully offline. No network needed.**
> 
> GitHub: <https://github.com/Henoch4/AuditTrailTrader>